{"school":{"dbn":"22K078","name":"J.H.S. 078 Roy H. Mann","boro":"Brooklyn","district":"22","district_label":"District 22","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":666,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"1420 EAST 68 STREET, BROOKLYN, NY 11234","phone":"718-693-3426","website":"www.RoyHMann.com","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/68586","accessibility":"Not Accessible","overview":"At Roy H. Mann, The School for Architectural Design and Innovative Technology, our mission is to provide all students with engaging, rigorous, and technology-based learning opportunities which align with the Next Generation Learning Standards. All classrooms are air-conditioned and feature a 65-inch LED flat panel SMART Board. Our students enjoy personalized attention from our dedicated grade teams. Every student has access to a full-time academic counselor, a vibrant and diverse arts program, and meaningful after-school activities. Teachers utilize ongoing assessment to collect data that informs instruction and meets the needs of each individual student, which leads to improved ELA and math skills. Through our Schoolwide Enrichment Model (SEM), students develop skills, foster positive relationships, and experience social growth. Our enrichment clusters, as well as our embedded organizational skills program, promote creativity and collaboration, in support of college- and career- readiness and community service. In partnership with staff, families, and the community, we foster the emotional, social, and intellectual growth of our students, in order to prepare them to reach their full academic potential and become outstanding citizens.","start_time":"08:00am","end_time":"02:19pm","languages":null,"subway":null,"bus":"B100, B3, B41, B47, BM1","shared_building":"0","neighborhood":"Georgetown","latitude":40.6208,"longitude":-73.9131,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","la